ll the  other thing kurt is it's it's 12 turns  in just over two miles that's what i  worry about for you are you worried are  you afraid does completely different  mean completely scary to you or you say  no i got this no i love it i actually  went and pre-ran the course  right before our wisconsin race a month  ago and you come off of one of the turns  and you're looking straight at the  museum and then we're on lake shore  drive and then you come back out onto  i think it's michigan ave and it just  has a great vibe all the way around and  that area is normally used for like  lollapalooza concerts so there's gonna  be so much extra action outside the race  hold on you pre-ran the race was this in  a rental car there's a rental car  i had a days of thunder i was wondering  about that too i was talking about that  too no no tires were harmed on that one  good now you mentioned it's it's going  to be a great vibe chicago is a great  sports  place like they love every sport from  football basketball baseball hockey  everything in in between what do you  hope this does for chicago  well it's to create the buzz for not  just the city but for our sport it  creates this ticket that people want to  come and be part of  and just be part of this i'm i've been  in this sport 23 years and this to me is  like one of those kid in a candy store  moments of i want to be part of this and  i'm glad that i'm having the chance to  drive next year for the team and  then i might be done driving after that  i was wondering whoa whoa whoa  i was wondering about that kurt because  you are 43 that's considered and no  offense that's considered older in your  business over the age of 40. when you  just said i might  be done after this do you really mean  that i was wondering do you have a game  plan about retiring so there's a few  different options and for me the team  which gave me so much respect about a  month ago they said you can drive as  long as you want to drive for us we  really a